=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ ANT @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt Apache Ant @VERSION@ for OpenVMS
1 'NOTICE
=prompt Apache Ant is under the Apache License 2.0; see [ANT]LICENSE.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [ANT]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for Apache Ant
    At system startup: to define ANT$ROOT at every boot, add this line to
    SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:ANT$STARTUP.COM
    For each user: to define the ANT command, add this line to LOGIN.COM:
    $ @ANT$ROOT:[000000]ANT$SETUP.COM
    Ant needs VSI OpenJDK 8 (SYS$STARTUP:OPENJDK$SETUP.COM).
    The manual is ANT$ROOT:[MANUAL]index.html.

PRODUCT REMOVE ANT removes the product and deassigns ANT$ROOT.
